1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,627
Welcome to Advanced Exploratory Data Analysis, course code Data two oh nine.

2
00:00:05,627 --> 00:00:09,107
This video is your roadmap to the whole course:

3
00:00:09,107 --> 00:00:18,288
what you will learn, how the fifteen weeks are organised, how you are assessed, which tools we use, and which books to read.

4
00:00:19,088 --> 00:00:24,333
Exploratory data analysis is a critical first step in analysing data.

5
00:00:24,333 --> 00:00:33,227
You explore the data to see what it seems to say, and look beneath the surface for insights using numbers and graphs.

6
00:00:33,227 --> 00:00:44,934
Careful analysis helps you detect mistakes, challenge assumptions, understand relationships between variables, and finally choose a good predictive model.

7
00:00:44,934 --> 00:00:47,822
This course takes a hands-on approach:

8
00:00:47,822 --> 00:00:54,512
you curate, pre-process and transform real datasets, and learn to explain your findings.

9
00:00:55,312 --> 00:01:02,273
The prerequisites are Data Visualization and Storytelling, and Probability and Statistics.

10
00:01:02,273 --> 00:01:06,373
The course is four credits, structured two zero four:

11
00:01:06,373 --> 00:01:14,031
two hours of lecture and four hours of lab each week, six contact hours in all, over fifteen weeks.

12
00:01:14,031 --> 00:01:20,992
That is thirty hours of theory and sixty hours of lab, so labs carry most of the learning.

13
00:01:21,792 --> 00:01:25,739
By the end you should be able to do four things.

14
00:01:25,739 --> 00:01:26,068
One:

15
00:01:26,068 --> 00:01:31,578
analyse the statistical and structural characteristics of datasets.

16
00:01:31,578 --> 00:01:31,906
Two:

17
00:01:31,906 --> 00:01:37,498
apply univariate, bivariate and multivariate exploratory techniques.

18
00:01:37,498 --> 00:01:37,992
Three:

19
00:01:37,992 --> 00:01:46,873
design and implement pre-processing and transformation strategies that improve data quality and reliability.

20
00:01:46,873 --> 00:01:47,613
And four:

21
00:01:47,613 --> 00:01:53,040
interpret your results to produce insights and support hypotheses.

22
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:56,169
The course has four modules.

23
00:01:56,169 --> 00:02:00,579
Module one, Statistical and Data Foundations for EDA:

24
00:02:00,579 --> 00:02:05,155
understand data structure and distributional behaviour.

25
00:02:05,155 --> 00:02:07,651
Module two, Core Advanced EDA:

26
00:02:07,651 --> 00:02:12,393
apply graphical and non-graphical exploratory techniques.

27
00:02:12,393 --> 00:02:17,551
Module three, Data Quality Engineering and Anomaly Management:

28
00:02:17,551 --> 00:02:20,629
create a reliable analytical dataset.

29
00:02:20,629 --> 00:02:27,119
And module four, Feature Engineering, Transformation and Analytical Structure:

30
00:02:27,119 --> 00:02:31,112
transform data and extract meaningful structure.

31
00:02:31,912 --> 00:02:34,277
Here is the week-by-week map.

32
00:02:34,277 --> 00:02:37,213
Weeks one to three cover module one.

33
00:02:37,213 --> 00:02:45,043
Weeks four to seven cover module two, and week seven includes the first assignment presentation.

34
00:02:45,043 --> 00:02:51,893
Weeks eight to eleven cover module three, with the second assignment in week eleven.

35
00:02:51,893 --> 00:02:55,319
Weeks twelve to fifteen cover module four.

36
00:02:55,319 --> 00:02:59,152
Week sixteen is the final project presentation.

37
00:02:59,952 --> 00:03:05,845
Assessment is seventy percent continuous and thirty percent final project.

38
00:03:05,845 --> 00:03:08,791
Laboratory assessment is ten percent.

39
00:03:08,791 --> 00:03:13,250
Assignments, which are mini projects, are fifty percent:

40
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:15,241
twenty five percent each.

41
00:03:15,241 --> 00:03:19,700
Class participation in lectures and labs is ten percent.

42
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,885
And the final project is thirty percent.

43
00:03:22,885 --> 00:03:34,272
Assignment one maps to outcomes one and two, assignment two to outcome three, and the lab assessment and final project cover all four outcomes.

44
00:03:35,072 --> 00:03:44,605
We use Excel, Python and R, with datasets and case studies from domains such as insurance, retail, pharma and healthcare.

45
00:03:44,605 --> 00:03:49,963
In these videos we use Python with pandas, seaborn and scikit-learn.

46
00:03:49,963 --> 00:04:01,465
Teaching methods include lectures, hands-on lab sessions, problem-solving through case studies, industry notebook reviews, and peer presentations.

47
00:04:01,465 --> 00:04:09,344
For self-learning, the Exploratory Data Analysis course by Johns Hopkins on Coursera is recommended.

48
00:04:10,144 --> 00:04:13,181
Here is how to use the video series.

49
00:04:13,181 --> 00:04:17,989
Watch the lecture first, then its lab, in syllabus order.

50
00:04:17,989 --> 00:04:24,401
Pause and run the notebook yourself, because you only learn EDA by doing it.

51
00:04:24,401 --> 00:04:29,209
Use the module revision videos before the lab assessment.

52
00:04:29,209 --> 00:04:35,536
And use the assignment and final project guides when you start those tasks.

53
00:04:36,336 --> 00:04:44,264
For further reading, the main textbooks are Making Sense of Data one and two by Myatt and Johnson.

54
00:04:44,264 --> 00:05:01,414
Useful references include Hands-On Exploratory Data Analysis with Python, Python for Data Analysis by Wes McKinney, the N I S T Engineering Statistics Handbook, and John Tukey's classic Exploratory Data Analysis.

55
00:05:01,414 --> 00:05:06,672
Read the chapter on exploratory data analysis before each module.

56
00:05:07,472 --> 00:05:08,473
To summarise:

57
00:05:08,473 --> 00:05:12,322
this course takes you through a complete workflow.

58
00:05:12,322 --> 00:05:31,800
You understand data and distributions, explore with numbers and graphs, clean and validate data, handle missing values and outliers, transform and engineer features, reduce dimensions, and finally build a trustworthy pipeline and report honest insights.

59
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:35,572
Start with lecture one, and I will see you there.

60
00:05:35,572 --> 00:05:37,112
Thanks for watching.

